  "protocol": {
    "scale": "joint_solved. Each frame's raw z gets its own scale and shift, solved jointly over the target and its sources from parallax under the GT poses; GT depth never enters the solver or the fusion",
    "poses": "oracle_gt. RGB-timestamp metric GT poses, used as an ORACLE by the solver and the fusion",
    "solver": "pim.fusion.joint_scale. About 1500 pixels per frame on a regular grid over finite raw z inside a 10% margin; every ordered pair; residual (z_in_j - depth_j) / (s_j * IQR of raw_z_j), the relative residual rescaled by depth_j / (s_j * IQR); soft L1 truncated at the visibility limit; ridge on (log s_k, t_k / median depth) toward the window mean; 15 by 15 shared grid, then Levenberg Marquardt with a numerical Jacobian at visibility limits x4, x2, x1. Low parallax windows keep the shared grid affine for every frame",
    "fusion": "the engine with the median aggregator and no front layer or edge options (rungb_<base> of the oracle edge group), with the target's own solved depth as the self layer; holes take that depth",
    "scoring": "the fused depth alone is aligned to the target GT by upstream compute_metrics' depth affine branch (the code evaluate_frame runs for rel_d), then rel_d and delta1_d x100 over GT-valid pixels and rel_d near, mid and far over GT depth thirds. baseline_self is the raw prediction scored the same way and must reproduce per_frame.csv",
    "oracle_diagnostic": "logging only. The oracle affine is the least squares fit of the cached GT-aligned depth on raw z. target_depth_error is the signed relative error of the solved depth at the target's median raw z pixel, window_depth_error the median of its absolute value over the window frames; scale_correlation is Pearson over targets of solved and oracle target scale",
    "oracle_comparison": "oracle_rel_d_median and oracle_rel_change_pct_median are read from the oracle edge summary for rungb_<base>; those scores fused GT-aligned sources and were NOT realigned after fusion, so they are an upper bound under a different protocol",
    "controls": "nofusion_joint_causal_adjacent_w4 scores only the target's own depth in its solved affine and must equal baseline_self; shuffled_poses_joint_causal_adjacent_w4 gives each source another random window frame's pose in both the solver and the fusion",
    "ridge_sensitivity": "ridge_low_change and ridge_high_change are the relative change of the target depth at its median raw z pixel when the solution is refined with the ridge weight times 0.1 and 10; the weight itself is fixed",
    "regression": "baseline_self equals per_frame.csv and nofusion equals baseline_self within 0.0001 (absolute, percent) for every target"
  },
